WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
 Hey, is their costume
cooler than mine, is it?

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:03.570
 What's this bit?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.320
I don't have that
bit on my costume.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.677
 Can I get that?

00:00:06.677 --> 00:00:17.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.195
 Oh, I'd like to fly.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:28.650
 Time travel?

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.970
Is that a superpower?

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.670
I'd love to go back and fix some
of these mistakes I've made.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:37.990
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:42.670
 I think they have such a
different outlook on the world.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.500
There's something about
opposites that attract.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.450
I think there's
something in Ikaris

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.280
that Sersi is just drawn to.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.890
There's something about the
way that Sersi sees the world

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.810
that Ikaris is drawn to.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.910
 I think they balance
each other beautifully

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:59.170
between the kind of practicality
and the duty and honor sense

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.800
that Ikaris has, balanced
between Sersi's way

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.700
that she sees
beauty in the world.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.000
And I think that's
what keeps them kind

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.400
of learning from each other.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.710
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.060
 God, I hate emojis.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.170
 The-- I know you--

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.690
 The smiley face.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.210
 You're going really
generic on that one.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.720
 I don't know any other ones.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.790
 The sunglasses
emoji, probably.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.360
And the sparkle emoji
to represent her powers.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.160
 For me it would
be, I think, the guy

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.730
with the stars in his eyes.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.025
Like, a hand going
one, like number one.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.060
 The rocket.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.170
The purple ball, where
you can talk to the beyond

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.270
because I talk to
the Celestials.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.330
Maybe the hands because
she heals with her hands.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:56.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.990
 Well, they came quite
with a blank canvas,

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.770
and it's really 7,000 years
of us influencing them.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.330
So who they are says a
lot about who we are.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.199
So in casting these ten
incredible individuals,

00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:12.440
I found unique individuals,
and hoping they

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.860
would open themselves up and
give us a sense of who they are

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.930
so we could shape the
character around who

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.770
they really are in real life.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:24.830
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.410
 Well, I thought that the--

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.650
this was supposed to be
the great female warrior,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.950
should fight like a
female and should have all

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.320
the grace and femininity
and that her strength

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.290
should come from that.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.590
Ballet is very
challenging, so I wanted

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.320
to set myself that
challenge, and hard for me

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.195
because I'm a bit impatient.

00:02:44.195 --> 00:02:49.840
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.410
 I think the most
excited one is my husband.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:57.730
When I met him, I was
already like 38, 39.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.730
And he said, "Oh, I want
you to be an action hero.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.100
Why don't you do a
movie Super Hero?"

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.720
And I'm like, "Baby,
forget about it.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.470
That's never going to happen."

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.700
And it did.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.500
And he's like, "See?

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.300
I told you."

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.870
Like, nothing.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.080
And I said, "It's a big deal.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:12.880
This is very

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.660
 I think the time
and place that

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.970
would have been my favorite
because the music was best,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.210
and it was just a
really cool period

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.660
of time and a cool place, was
probably London in the 1960s.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.860
 I would live in
the medieval times

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.400
if I were able to be like
a princess or something.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.810
I think that would be cool.
- Fair enough.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.610
 Yeah.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.100
 I think I'm going
to go to ancient China

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.270
to see my ancestors.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.330
That would be fun.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:44.890
 I've got to say 5,000
years ago because not

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.350
too much things to worry about.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.983
 When things were
kind of raw and human.

00:03:48.983 --> 00:03:50.050
There wasn't as much technology.

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:55.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.840
 Surreal.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.660
I mean, yeah, I remember
seeing you for the first time,

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.550
looking you up and down.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.450
 I think, it was really
cool, but everyone was also

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.910
kind of scoping each
other out, like, hey,

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.430
is their costume cooler
than mine, is it?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.280
 What's this bit?

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.640
I don't have that
bit on my costume.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.770
 Why have you got this bit?

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:14.800
Can I get that?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.380
So it was really exciting
and funny, but the costumes

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.839
we kind of built over
a long period of time

00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:21.130
into what's best
for the character

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.800
and also what's going to
be practical for shooting.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.040
They're not just a, oh let's put
on this because it looks cool.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.650
It's like OK well, how
does that one interact

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.135
with your specific superpowers?

00:04:31.135 --> 00:04:36.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.970
 I honestly love doing
the action sequences.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.920
I found it very
challenging, but I've

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.310
never gotten the opportunity
to do action like that before.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.750
And so I just, honestly
while shooting it,

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.010
those parts were challenging.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.900
Watching it on screen,
how well it came together,

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.250
that was my favorite part.

